Agreement.”
4.
Section 8 -- Special Provisions.  Section 8 of the Agreement is hereby amended by:
•
Deleting the third sentence of Section 8(i) and replacing it with the following: “The
broker/dealer, bank or trust company selected by the City shall be the custodian of the Assets,
and such person shall constitute a “qualified custodian” as such term is defined in Rule 206(4)-
2 under the Investment Advisers Act of 1940, as amended.”
•
Adding the following at the end of Section 8(ii): “Advisor may select broker-dealers providing
research or brokerage services to Advisor, may use these research or brokerage services for
its benefit, for the benefit of the Assets in the Account, or for other clients’ accounts, and may
pay a greater commission on trades than another broker-dealer might have charged, all
consistent with Advisor’s applicable policies and procedures, its duty to seek best execution
and applicable law.”
•
Adding the following sentence at the end of Section 8(iv): “For the avoidance of doubt, the
City authorizes the Advisor to disclose its confidential information to any Service Providers
(defined below) engaged by the Advisor to assist the Advisor in meeting its duties and
obligations under this Agreement as set forth in Section 10 hereto.”
•
Deleting the third sentence of Section 8(v) and replacing it with the following: “Except for bad
faith, intentional misconduct, gross negligence, or violation of any federal, state, or local law
or professional standard of care in regard of the Advisor’s performance of its duties under this
Agreement, neither the Advisor nor any of its directors, officers, employees or agents shall be
liable for any acts or omissions or for any loss suffered by the Account.”
•
Adding the following as a new Section 8(vii): “Proxy Voting. Unless otherwise retained by the
City, the Advisor or its delegate or agent shall be responsible for voting proxies and taking
action with respect to corporate actions on behalf of the Account. The Advisor will vote all
such proxies (or direct its proxy voting service to vote all such proxies) in accordance with the
Advisor’s proxy voting guidelines and procedures in effect from time to time as described in
the Advisor’s Form ADV, Part 2.  The Advisor has no liability to the City, and the City will
indemnify the Advisor for any loss that arises from or in connection with any recommendation
made by the Advisor with respect to the voting of proxies or voluntary corporate actions. In no
event will the Advisor have any responsibilities for the Assets or the Account with respect to
bankruptcies, class actions or other litigation relating to the Assets.”
•
Adding the following as a new Section 8(viii): “No Guarantee. The Advisor gives no warranty
and does not guarantee: (a) the performance of the Assets; (b) that the Advisor’s investment
advice will be successful; or (c) that any one or more specific individuals will be responsible
for supplying services hereunder.”
5.
Section 9 -- General Provisions.  Section 9 is hereby amended by:
•
Revising clause (2) of Section 9(iv) as follows: “or (2) any act constituting gross negligence
or an otherwise wrongful act, error or omission by the Advisor, or its employees or sub-
Advisors in the performance of this Agreement.”
```

